# Multi-Lane Configuration

- Treat `Mines-Checkpoint` lanes as independent hardware contexts inside one
  process.
- Preserve unique per-lane Modbus controller, RFID reader, RFID listen port,
  display topic/IP, camera, and workflow settings.
- `checkpoint-config` canonical layout profiles are `checkpoint` and
  `weighbridge`; legacy IDs may normalize to those families.
- Do not assume a lane label creates a distinct business/API profile. Verify
  the RFID-selected flow and configured endpoint contract.
- Before changing a lane, inspect the complete lane object and validate that
  ports and topics do not collide.
- Do not copy credentials from local configuration into docs, tests, or logs.
